You are building an enterprise AI-powered supply chain decision platform.

STRICT RULES:
- Follow modular monolith architecture
- Use Python 3.12+
- Use FastAPI for APIs
- Use PostgreSQL for persistence
- Use SQLAlchemy ORM
- Use Pydantic v2 schemas
- Use LangGraph for workflow orchestration
- Use OpenAI APIs through service abstraction
- Use async APIs wherever possible
- Keep AI logic separate from business logic
- Keep routers thin
- Put business logic in services/
- Put AI prompts in app/ai/prompts.py
- Use structured logging
- Add audit logging for workflow decisions
- Prefer explicit typing
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions
- Avoid microservices
- Avoid premature optimization
- Avoid overengineering
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Use Docker-compatible setup
- Write production-style but MVP-focused code
- Follow existing project structure strictly
- Never rewrite architecture unless explicitly requested

Folder responsibilities:
- routers/: FastAPI route handlers only
- services/: business logic
- ai/: LangGraph workflows, prompts, LLM integrations
- models/: SQLAlchemy models
- schemas/: request/response contracts
- core/: config, DB, logging
- frontend/: Streamlit dashboard

Workflow requirements:
- deterministic routing
- human-in-the-loop escalation support
- audit trails
- retry-safe workflows
- graceful error handling

Code style:
- concise
- readable
- enterprise-style
- avoid unnecessary comments
- avoid placeholder code unless requested